I'm rather new to this whole thing, so any stupid questions I ask are out of
ignorance.  Bear with me..

I was running through the Dungeons of Doom (whee!) with a Valkyrie wearing a
couple of mostly uninteresting items.  (Well, except for the +1 cloak of
invisibilty.)  Anyway, I came across a 'f' and, thinking it was my pet kitten,
didn't attack it.  The jaguar hit me first.  (Ouch!)  The strange thing was,
though, that I got a message along the lines of "You feel yourself polymorph
into a hill orc" or something like that within the next turn or two.  Now, I
know I didn't have a ring of polymorph at the time, I will swear up and down
that I have never seen a chameleon, and there were neither traps in the room
nor people who could be slinging wands of polymorph at me.  So was this a
function of the jaguar (which I find somewhat puzzling), or something else
that I haven't even considered yet?

Completely unrelated question: I had a chaotic character lucky enough to
free a water demon while drinking from a fountain, who granted my (eventually)
hapless character a wish.  I decided a blessed rustproof +3 Stormbringer
might be nice.  Unfortunately, I noticed that afterward, even though I had
the safe_pet option set, that I would hit my kitten rather than displace
the poor thing or stop.  I'm assuming this is a function of Stormy, but...
is it a bug, or a feature?

